From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:01:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: add the MT6797 power sequence

The vendor brings the T880 up as GPU LDOs, VGPU, VCG, MFG_ASYNC, MFG, cores,
BG3D, 100 us, bus protection release, async timing. Panfrost starts at the
domains and has no LDO or protection step, so powering the domains from it
alone would run them with no rail and no SRAM supply.

Add callbacks before the domains, after the clocks, before the clocks stop and
after the domains, and use them on MT6797. The first resolves every provider
before any effect, so a load without the regulator or clock module defers with
the hardware untouched. It refuses a hot SoC or a rail not at 1.0 V, selects
a running clock, programs the LDOs with readback, pulses the TOPRGU reset,
asserts protection, and enables the LDOs and the rail.

This is a fixed point with no OPP table. The GPU clock parent is clk26m, or
syspll_d3 through a module parameter, and is refused above 365 MHz. MFGPLL is
not touched. Runtime suspend is held off, so the domains cycle only at unbind.

This keeps all of it in the module, so it can be changed without a boot.
---
